    "result_text": "The full suite is green \u2014 **36 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors, BUILD SUCCESS**.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented per-country national-number length validation for E.164 telephone numbers in `OwnerRestControllerV1.normalizeTelephone`.\n\n**What I found:** The telephone E.164 normalization already lives in `OwnerRestControllerV1.normalizeTelephone` (line 344). It strips non-digits, applies the default `+61` country code for national-format numbers, and enforced only the general \"8\u201315 digits after the `+`\" bound. It had no per-country length rule.\n\n**The change** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n- Added a `NATIONAL_NUMBER_LENGTHS` map: `+61` \u2192 9 national digits, `+1` \u2192 10.\n- Added `validateNationalNumberLength(...)`, called after the 8\u201315 bound. It matches the country code by **longest known prefix**, then rejects with **400** when the national digits following that code don't match the required count. Country codes not in the map (e.g. `+64`) keep only the general bound, so `+64 21 123 456` \u2192 `+6421123456` remains accepted.\n\n**Verification:**\n- `Cp26` (`+61 123` \u2192 400) passes.\n- Regression checks stay green: `Cp02`/`Cp08` (`0412 345 678` \u2192 `+61412345678`, 9 national digits), `Cp08` (`+64\u2026` accepted), `Cp03` (duplicate across formats \u2192 409). The base `uniqueTelephone()` (`04########` \u2192 9 national digits under `+61`) still validates.\n- Full suite: 36/36 passing.",
